IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Cat Act 2011 (Western Australia) -- what the owner of a cat must do: register it, tag it, microchip it and have it
-- sterilised once it reaches 6 months of age (ss 5, 6, 14, 18), with the exemptions; who is an owner (s 4); when a
-- registration must be refused (s 9(2)-(4)); the registration fee and period (Cat Regulations 2012 reg 12, Sch 3);
-- giving a cat away or selling it (s 23, reg 19); telling the local government of a change (s 25); the number of cats
-- that may be kept (s 79(3)(h) and the Cat (Uniform Local Provisions) Regulations 2013 regs 5-7); and the fines.
--
-- SEAT: the cat owner -- "What must I do before my cat is six months old?" Every decision is phrased as the owner would
-- ask it: "Am I the owner of this cat", "Must I have my cat registered", "Must I have my cat microchipped", "Must I have
-- my cat sterilised", "How much is the registration fee", "When does my cat's registration end", "How many cats may I
-- keep here".
--
-- Provisions covered: Act ss 3 (microchipped, sterilised, registered, transfer), 4(1)-(2), 5(1)-(2), 6(1)-(2),
-- 9(2)-(4), 14(1)-(3), 18(1)-(3), 23(1)-(2), 25, 79(3)(h) and the "Penalty" lines; Cat Regulations 2012 regs 8, 9, 10,
-- 12, 19, Sch 2 items 1, 2, 4, 6, 8, 9, 11 and Sch 3; Cat (Uniform Local Provisions) Regulations 2013 regs 4-7, 13(1).
--
-- Edition: Cat Act 2011 compilation 00-l0-01 (amendments to No. 29 of 2021 in force; the Dog Amendment (Stop Puppy
-- Farming) Act 2021 ss 50-61 and the Evidence Act 2025 s 492(1) uncommenced), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/cat-act-2011-00-l0-01.txt (retrieved 7 September 2026). Cat Regulations 2012
-- compilation 02-b0-00 (amendments to SL 2025/138, in force 24 July 2025), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/cat-regulations-2012.txt. Cat (Uniform Local Provisions) Regulations 2013 compilation
-- 00-a0-05, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/cat-uniform-local-provisions-regulations-2013.txt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 7 (interfering with a tag), ss 8, 10-13 (the application, cancellation, certificates and tags, the
-- register, notice of decisions), s 9(5)-(6) (documents the local government may ask for), ss 15-17 and 19-21 (duties
-- of implanters, database companies and veterinarians), s 24 (the seller's notice of transfer), Part 3 (control
-- notices, seizure, cat management facilities, breeding approvals, prizes), Part 4 (administration, enforcement,
-- infringement procedure, objections and review), the s 6(3) defence, reg 13 (moving district), reg 15 (tag colours),
-- local laws themselves (only their number limit is an input), ULP regs 8-12 (applying for more cats; the transitional
-- defence). Machinery out: ss 1, 2, 42-48, 76-88.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cat Act 2011 -- the cat owner's questions`

§§ `s 4 -- am I the owner`

-- s 4(1): "owner, in relation to a cat, means any of these persons -- (a) in the case of a cat that is registered, the
-- registered owner of the cat; or (b) in the case of a cat that is not registered, a person who, or an owner of a
-- business or organisation that, ordinarily keeps and cares for the cat; or (c) if a person referred to in paragraph
-- (b) is a child under 18 years of age, that child's parent or guardian."
-- s 4(2): for a cat that is not registered but is microchipped, the person "recorded as the owner of the cat in a
-- microchip database is to be taken, in the absence of evidence to the contrary," to ordinarily keep and care for it.
DECLARE `How I stand to the cat` IS ONE OF
    `I am the person it is registered to`                 -- registered owner: the person in whose name it is registered
    `I ordinarily keep and care for it`                   -- s 4(1)(b), including through my business or organisation
    `my child under 18 ordinarily keeps and cares for it` -- s 4(1)(c): I am that child's parent or guardian
    `my name is on its microchip database record`         -- s 4(2)
    `none of these`

@export Am I the owner of this cat under the Cat Act 2011 (WA) s 4?
GIVEN `how I stand` IS A `How I stand to the cat` @desc How you are connected to the cat
      `the cat is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cat is registered with a local government under s 9
      `there is evidence I do not keep it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a database record only: whether there is evidence that you do not in fact ordinarily keep and care for the cat
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I the owner of this cat` IF
    CONSIDER `how I stand`
    WHEN `I am the person it is registered to` THEN `the cat is registered`
    WHEN `I ordinarily keep and care for it` THEN NOT `the cat is registered`
    WHEN `my child under 18 ordinarily keeps and cares for it` THEN NOT `the cat is registered`
    WHEN `my name is on its microchip database record` THEN (NOT `the cat is registered`) AND (NOT `there is evidence I do not keep it`)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `ss 5(1), 14(1), 18(1) -- the day my cat reaches 6 months of age`

-- Each duty falls on "the owner of a cat that has reached 6 months of age". The Act does not say when a cat born on
-- the 29th, 30th or 31st of a month reaches 6 months if the sixth month has no such day. INFERENCE: it has reached
-- 6 months once that month has ended without the day, that is, on the 1st of the following month.
GIVEN `my cat's date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the same day 6 months on` MEANS
    Date (DATE_DAY `my cat's date of birth`) (DATE_MONTH `my cat's date of birth` PLUS 6) (DATE_YEAR `my cat's date of birth`)

@export On what day does my cat reach 6 months of age (Cat Act 2011 (WA) ss 5, 14, 18)?
GIVEN `my cat's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your cat's date of birth, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `When does my cat reach 6 months of age` IS
    IF DATE_DAY (`the same day 6 months on` `my cat's date of birth`) EQUALS DATE_DAY `my cat's date of birth`
        THEN `the same day 6 months on` `my cat's date of birth`
        ELSE Date 1 (DATE_MONTH `my cat's date of birth` PLUS 7) (DATE_YEAR `my cat's date of birth`)

GIVEN `my cat's date of birth` IS A DATE, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my cat has reached 6 months of age` IF
    NOT (`the day` LESS THAN `When does my cat reach 6 months of age` `my cat's date of birth`)

§§ `s 5 and reg 9 -- registration`

-- s 5(1): "The owner of a cat that has reached 6 months of age must ensure that the cat is registered with the local
-- government in whose district the cat is ordinarily kept. Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
-- s 5(2): "Subsection (1) does not apply if -- (a) the cat has been kept by the person for less than 14 days; or (b) the
-- person has been resident in the State for less than 14 days; or (c) the cat belongs to a class of cats prescribed as
-- exempt from registration."
-- reg 9(2): exempt is a cat "in the custody of" Cat Haven, the RSPCA WA, the Commonwealth department administering the
-- Biosecurity Act 2015, a cat management facility, or veterinary premises. reg 9(3): a cat in foster care placed by
-- Cat Haven or the RSPCA WA, or by a SAFE entity "provided that the cat has not been in foster care for more than a
-- total of 12 weeks".
DECLARE `Where my cat is` IS ONE OF
    `at home with me`
    `in the custody of Cat Haven`
    `in the custody of the RSPCA WA`
    `in the custody of the Commonwealth biosecurity department`
    `in the custody of a cat management facility`
    `at veterinary premises`
    `in foster care placed by Cat Haven or the RSPCA WA`
    `in foster care placed by a SAFE entity`

GIVEN `where my cat is` IS A `Where my cat is`, `weeks in SAFE foster care` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my cat is in a class exempt from registration` IF
    CONSIDER `where my cat is`
    WHEN `at home with me` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `in foster care placed by a SAFE entity` THEN `weeks in SAFE foster care` AT MOST 12
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE `Registration duty` IS ONE OF
    `no: my cat is not yet 6 months old (s 5(1))`
    `no: I have kept the cat for less than 14 days (s 5(2)(a))`
    `no: I have been resident in the State for less than 14 days (s 5(2)(b))`
    `no: my cat is in a class exempt from registration (s 5(2)(c), reg 9)`
    `yes, and it is registered: keep the registration current (s 5(1))`
    `yes: register it with the local government of the district where it is ordinarily kept (s 5(1))`

-- "kept by the person for less than 14 days" is asked as a count of whole days (the day the keeping began not counted).
@export Must I have my cat registered (Cat Act 2011 (WA) s 5)?
GIVEN `my cat's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your cat's date of birth, ISO 8601
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about, ISO 8601
      `days I have kept the cat` IS A NUMBER @desc How many whole days you have kept the cat
      `days I have lived in WA` IS A NUMBER @desc How many whole days you have been resident in Western Australia
      `where my cat is` IS A `Where my cat is` @desc Where the cat is, or who has custody of it
      `weeks in SAFE foster care` IS A NUMBER @desc If in foster care placed by a SAFE entity: total weeks in foster care
      `my cat is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cat is now registered with that local government
GIVETH A `Registration duty`
DECIDE `Must I have my cat registered` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `my cat has reached 6 months of age` `my cat's date of birth` `the day`
            THEN `no: my cat is not yet 6 months old (s 5(1))`
        IF `days I have kept the cat` LESS THAN 14
            THEN `no: I have kept the cat for less than 14 days (s 5(2)(a))`
        IF `days I have lived in WA` LESS THAN 14
            THEN `no: I have been resident in the State for less than 14 days (s 5(2)(b))`
        IF `my cat is in a class exempt from registration` `where my cat is` `weeks in SAFE foster care`
            THEN `no: my cat is in a class exempt from registration (s 5(2)(c), reg 9)`
        IF `my cat is registered`
            THEN `yes, and it is registered: keep the registration current (s 5(1))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: register it with the local government of the district where it is ordinarily kept (s 5(1))`

§§ `s 6 and reg 10 -- the registration tag`

-- s 6(1): "The owner of a registered cat must ensure that when the cat is in a public place the cat is wearing its
-- registration tag. Penalty: a fine of $5 000." (2): not for a class prescribed as exempt. reg 10(2): the owner of a cat
-- "that is being exhibited" at a show held by one of the four named cat bodies (or an affiliate) is exempt "but only
-- while that cat is being exhibited". "public place means any place to which the public has lawful access" (s 3).
@export Must my cat be wearing its registration tag (Cat Act 2011 (WA) s 6)?
GIVEN `my cat is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cat is registered
      `my cat is in a public place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cat is in a place to which the public has lawful access
      `my cat is being exhibited at a recognised cat show` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cat is being exhibited at a show held by one of the cat bodies named in reg 10(1), or an affiliate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my cat be wearing its tag` IF
        `my cat is registered`
    AND `my cat is in a public place`
    AND (NOT `my cat is being exhibited at a recognised cat show`)

§§ `s 14 -- microchipping`

-- s 14(1): "The owner of a cat that has reached 6 months of age must ensure that the cat is microchipped, unless the cat
-- is exempt from microchipping. Penalty: a fine of $5 000." (2): exempt if a veterinarian's certificate "stating that
-- the implantation of a microchip in the cat may adversely affect the health and welfare of the cat applies". (3): such
-- a certificate "cannot apply in respect of a cat that is under 6 months of age". "microchipped means implanted with a
-- microchip in a prescribed manner" (s 3): by a microchip implanter (reg 8), that is a veterinarian, a veterinary nurse
-- or a person with the reg 7(2) qualifications.
DECLARE `Microchip duty` IS ONE OF
    `no: my cat is not yet 6 months old (s 14(1))`
    `no: a veterinarian's certificate exempts my cat (s 14(2))`
    `yes, and it is microchipped (s 14(1))`
    `yes: have it microchipped by a microchip implanter (s 14(1), reg 8)`

GIVEN `my cat's date of birth` IS A DATE, `the day` IS A DATE, `a vet has certified a microchip may harm my cat` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my cat is exempt from microchipping` IF
        `a vet has certified a microchip may harm my cat`
    AND `my cat has reached 6 months of age` `my cat's date of birth` `the day`

@export Must I have my cat microchipped (Cat Act 2011 (WA) s 14)?
GIVEN `my cat's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your cat's date of birth, ISO 8601
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about, ISO 8601
      `my cat is microchipped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cat has been implanted with a microchip by a microchip implanter
      `a vet has certified a microchip may harm my cat` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a veterinarian's certificate says implanting a microchip may adversely affect the cat's health and welfare
GIVETH A `Microchip duty`
DECIDE `Must I have my cat microchipped` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `my cat has reached 6 months of age` `my cat's date of birth` `the day`
            THEN `no: my cat is not yet 6 months old (s 14(1))`
        IF `my cat is exempt from microchipping` `my cat's date of birth` `the day` `a vet has certified a microchip may harm my cat`
            THEN `no: a veterinarian's certificate exempts my cat (s 14(2))`
        IF `my cat is microchipped`
            THEN `yes, and it is microchipped (s 14(1))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: have it microchipped by a microchip implanter (s 14(1), reg 8)`

§§ `s 18 -- sterilisation`

-- s 18(1): "The owner of a cat that has reached 6 months of age must ensure that the cat is sterilised by a
-- veterinarian, unless the cat is exempt from sterilisation. Penalty: a fine of $5 000." (2): exempt if "(a) a
-- certificate given by a veterinarian stating that to sterilise the cat may adversely affect the health and welfare of
-- the cat applies ...; (b) the cat is owned, for the purpose of breeding, by an approved cat breeder; (c) the cat belongs
-- to a class of cats prescribed as exempt from sterilisation." (3): the certificate "cannot apply" under 6 months.
-- No class is prescribed under (2)(c): the Cat Regulations 2012 as deposited prescribe none.
-- "sterilised means made permanently infertile by a surgical procedure" (s 3).
DECLARE `Sterilisation duty` IS ONE OF
    `no: my cat is not yet 6 months old (s 18(1))`
    `no: a veterinarian's certificate exempts my cat (s 18(2)(a))`
    `no: I am an approved cat breeder and own it for breeding (s 18(2)(b))`
    `yes, and it is sterilised (s 18(1))`
    `yes: have it sterilised by a veterinarian (s 18(1))`

GIVEN `my cat's date of birth` IS A DATE, `the day` IS A DATE
      `a vet has certified sterilising may harm my cat` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am an approved breeder keeping it for breeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my cat is exempt from sterilisation` IF
        (`a vet has certified sterilising may harm my cat` AND `my cat has reached 6 months of age` `my cat's date of birth` `the day`)
    OR  `I am an approved breeder keeping it for breeding`

@export Must I have my cat sterilised (Cat Act 2011 (WA) s 18)?
GIVEN `my cat's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your cat's date of birth, ISO 8601
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about, ISO 8601
      `my cat is sterilised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cat has been made permanently infertile by surgery by a veterinarian
      `a vet has certified sterilising may harm my cat` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a veterinarian's certificate says sterilising may adversely affect the cat's health and welfare
      `I am an approved breeder keeping it for breeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold an approval to breed cats under s 37 and own this cat for breeding
GIVETH A `Sterilisation duty`
DECIDE `Must I have my cat sterilised` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `my cat has reached 6 months of age` `my cat's date of birth` `the day`
            THEN `no: my cat is not yet 6 months old (s 18(1))`
        IF `I am an approved breeder keeping it for breeding`
            THEN `no: I am an approved cat breeder and own it for breeding (s 18(2)(b))`
        IF `my cat is exempt from sterilisation` `my cat's date of birth` `the day` `a vet has certified sterilising may harm my cat` `I am an approved breeder keeping it for breeding`
            THEN `no: a veterinarian's certificate exempts my cat (s 18(2)(a))`
        IF `my cat is sterilised`
            THEN `yes, and it is sterilised (s 18(1))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: have it sterilised by a veterinarian (s 18(1))`

§§ `s 9(2)-(4) -- must my application be refused`

-- s 9(2): the local government "must refuse an application for the grant or renewal of the registration of a cat if,
-- and only if, the local government is satisfied that one or more of the following apply -- (a) the applicant is a child
-- under 18 years of age; (b) the cat belongs to a class of cats prescribed as exempt from registration; (c) the cat is
-- not microchipped; (d) the cat is not sterilised; (e) the applicant has been convicted within the previous 3 years of
-- 2 or more offences against" this Act, the Dog Act 1976 or the Animal Welfare Act 2002.
-- (3), (4): it "must not refuse" a cat that is not microchipped, or not sterilised, if the cat is exempt "as referred to
-- in section 14(2)" or "section 18(2)".
-- The grounds turn on what the local government is satisfied of. Each input is a fact the local government is
-- satisfied of; the answer is conditional on that.
DECLARE `Registration outcome` IS ONE OF
    `refused: I am under 18 (s 9(2)(a))`
    `refused: my cat is in a class exempt from registration (s 9(2)(b))`
    `refused: my cat is not microchipped (s 9(2)(c))`
    `refused: my cat is not sterilised (s 9(2)(d))`
    `refused: 2 or more convictions within the previous 3 years (s 9(2)(e))`
    `not to be refused, if the local government is satisfied of none of the s 9(2) grounds`

@export Must the local government refuse to register my cat (Cat Act 2011 (WA) s 9)?
GIVEN `my cat's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your cat's date of birth, ISO 8601
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the application is decided, ISO 8601
      `I am under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, the applicant, are under 18
      `where my cat is` IS A `Where my cat is` @desc Where the cat is, or who has custody of it
      `weeks in SAFE foster care` IS A NUMBER @desc If in foster care placed by a SAFE entity: total weeks in foster care
      `my cat is microchipped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cat is microchipped
      `a vet has certified a microchip may harm my cat` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a veterinarian's certificate exempts the cat from microchipping
      `my cat is sterilised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cat is sterilised
      `a vet has certified sterilising may harm my cat` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a veterinarian's certificate exempts the cat from sterilisation
      `I am an approved breeder keeping it for breeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an approved cat breeder owning this cat for breeding
      `my convictions in the last 3 years` IS A NUMBER @desc How many offences against the Cat Act, Dog Act 1976 or Animal Welfare Act 2002 you have been convicted of in the previous 3 years
GIVETH A `Registration outcome`
DECIDE `Must my registration be refused` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `I am under 18`
            THEN `refused: I am under 18 (s 9(2)(a))`
        IF `my cat is in a class exempt from registration` `where my cat is` `weeks in SAFE foster care`
            THEN `refused: my cat is in a class exempt from registration (s 9(2)(b))`
        IF (NOT `my cat is microchipped`) AND (NOT `my cat is exempt from microchipping` `my cat's date of birth` `the day` `a vet has certified a microchip may harm my cat`)
            THEN `refused: my cat is not microchipped (s 9(2)(c))`
        IF (NOT `my cat is sterilised`) AND (NOT `my cat is exempt from sterilisation` `my cat's date of birth` `the day` `a vet has certified sterilising may harm my cat` `I am an approved breeder keeping it for breeding`)
            THEN `refused: my cat is not sterilised (s 9(2)(d))`
        IF `my convictions in the last 3 years` AT LEAST 2
            THEN `refused: 2 or more convictions within the previous 3 years (s 9(2)(e))`
        OTHERWISE `not to be refused, if the local government is satisfied of none of the s 9(2) grounds`

§§ `Cat Regulations 2012 Sch 3 -- the registration fee`

-- Sch 3 cl 1(2) Table: item 1, one year, "(a) if application is for grant of registration and is made after 31 May for
-- registration until the next 31 October" $10.00, "(b) otherwise" $20.00; item 2, 3 years, $42.50; item 3, life,
-- $100.00. cl 1(3): "if the owner of a cat is a pensioner" (an eligible pensioner under the Rates and Charges (Rebates
-- and Deferments) Act 1992 s 3(1), asked as a fact), the fee "is 50% of the fee that would otherwise be payable".
-- cl 1(4): a local government "may reduce or waive" a fee, so the figure is the most I can be charged.
-- READING: "after 31 May" is read as an application made from 1 June to 31 October -- a grant made in November or
-- December buys more than ten months and is not the late-year half fee.
DECLARE `Registration term` IS ONE OF
    `one year`
    `3 years`
    `the life of the cat`

@export What is the most the registration fee for my cat can be, in dollars (Cat Regulations 2012 Sch 3)?
GIVEN `the term` IS A `Registration term` @desc Registration for one year, 3 years or the life of the cat (reg 12(1))
      `it is a renewal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are renewing an existing registration rather than applying for a first grant
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you make the application, ISO 8601
      `I am a pensioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an eligible pensioner under the Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most my registration fee can be` IS
    IF `I am a pensioner` THEN `the full fee` TIMES 0.5 ELSE `the full fee`
    WHERE
        `the full fee` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the term`
            WHEN `one year` THEN
                IF      (NOT `it is a renewal`)
                    AND DATE_MONTH `the day I apply` AT LEAST 6
                    AND DATE_MONTH `the day I apply` AT MOST 10
                THEN 10 ELSE 20
            WHEN `3 years` THEN 42.5
            WHEN `the life of the cat` THEN 100

§§ `Cat Regulations 2012 reg 12 -- how long registration lasts`

-- reg 12(2)(a): registration has effect from the period in the certificate "until -- (i) in the case of registration
-- for one year -- the next 31 October, unless cancelled sooner; or (ii) in the case of registration for 3 years -- 31
-- October in the final year of that period, unless cancelled sooner; or (iii) in the case of registration for the life
-- of the cat -- the death of the cat, unless cancelled sooner".
-- READINGS: a registration taking effect on 31 October runs to the following 31 October (one that expires the day it
-- starts is absurd); a 3-year registration runs to the third 31 October, counting registration years.
DECLARE `When registration ends` IS ONE OF
    `on 31 October`
        HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `on the death of the cat, unless cancelled sooner`

GIVEN `the day it takes effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the next 31 October` MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH `the day it takes effect` AT MOST 9 OR (DATE_MONTH `the day it takes effect` EQUALS 10 AND DATE_DAY `the day it takes effect` LESS THAN 31)
        THEN Date 31 10 (DATE_YEAR `the day it takes effect`)
        ELSE Date 31 10 (DATE_YEAR `the day it takes effect` PLUS 1)

@export When does my cat's registration end (Cat Regulations 2012 reg 12)?
GIVEN `the term` IS A `Registration term` @desc Registration for one year, 3 years or the life of the cat
      `the day it takes effect` IS A DATE @desc The day the registration takes effect, from the registration certificate, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `When registration ends`
DECIDE `When does my cat's registration end` IS
    CONSIDER `the term`
    WHEN `one year` THEN `on 31 October` (`the next 31 October` `the day it takes effect`)
    WHEN `3 years` THEN `on 31 October` (Date 31 10 (DATE_YEAR (`the next 31 October` `the day it takes effect`) PLUS 2))
    WHEN `the life of the cat` THEN `on the death of the cat, unless cancelled sooner`

-- reg 12(2)(b): registration "may be renewed to take effect as from 1 November in any year, within the preceding
-- period of 21 days" -- 11 to 31 October.
@export Can I renew my cat's registration today so that it takes effect from 1 November (Cat Regulations 2012 reg 12(2)(b))?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day you would renew, ISO 8601
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I renew today to take effect from 1 November` IF
    DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 10 AND DATE_DAY `the day` AT LEAST 11

§§ `s 23 and reg 19 -- giving my cat away or selling it`

-- s 23(1): "A person must not transfer a cat that is not microchipped unless, at the time of the transfer, the person is
-- satisfied that a certificate referred to in section 14(2) applies". (2): nor a cat that is not sterilised unless the
-- person is satisfied that "(i) a certificate referred to in section 18(2)(a) applies ...; or (ii) the purchaser is an
-- approved cat breeder and the purchaser is purchasing the cat for the purpose of breeding; or (iii)" a prescribed
-- class (none is prescribed), "or (b) a voucher is given to the purchaser by the person to enable the purchaser to
-- have the cat sterilised at a later date by a veterinarian at no cost to the purchaser". Penalty $5 000 each.
-- "transfer ... includes -- (a) sell, trade, give away, take consideration for, transfer ownership of and offer for
-- sale" (s 3). reg 19: s 23(1) and (2) "do not apply if a cat is being transferred to an organisation or person set out
-- in regulation 9" -- read as the bodies named in reg 9 (Cat Haven, the RSPCA WA, the SAFE entities, the Commonwealth
-- department, a cat management facility, veterinary premises), not a foster carer.
-- s 23 has no 6-month threshold: it reaches a kitten.
DECLARE `Transfer answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the transfer is to a body named in reg 9 (reg 19)`
    `not unless it is microchipped first (s 23(1))`
    `not unless it is sterilised first, or I give the new owner a free sterilisation voucher (s 23(2))`
    `yes (s 23)`

@export May I give away or sell my cat (Cat Act 2011 (WA) s 23)?
GIVEN `to a body named in reg 9` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are transferring the cat to Cat Haven, the RSPCA WA, a SAFE entity, a cat management facility, veterinary premises or the Commonwealth biosecurity department
      `my cat is microchipped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cat is microchipped
      `a vet's microchip certificate applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are satisfied a veterinarian's certificate under s 14(2) applies to the cat
      `my cat is sterilised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cat is sterilised
      `a vet's sterilisation certificate applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are satisfied a veterinarian's certificate under s 18(2)(a) applies to the cat
      `the new owner is an approved breeder buying it to breed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the new owner is an approved cat breeder taking the cat for breeding
      `I give a free sterilisation voucher` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you give the new owner a voucher to have the cat sterilised later by a veterinarian at no cost to them
GIVETH A `Transfer answer`
DECIDE `May I give away or sell my cat` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `to a body named in reg 9`
            THEN `yes: the transfer is to a body named in reg 9 (reg 19)`
        IF (NOT `my cat is microchipped`) AND (NOT `a vet's microchip certificate applies`)
            THEN `not unless it is microchipped first (s 23(1))`
        IF      (NOT `my cat is sterilised`)
            AND (NOT `a vet's sterilisation certificate applies`)
            AND (NOT `the new owner is an approved breeder buying it to breed`)
            AND (NOT `I give a free sterilisation voucher`)
            THEN `not unless it is sterilised first, or I give the new owner a free sterilisation voucher (s 23(2))`
        OTHERWISE `yes (s 23)`

§§ `s 25 -- telling them of a change`

-- s 25: "The owner of a cat must give notice in writing -- (a) to the local government with which the cat is registered,
-- if there is a change to any of the information prescribed under section 12(3) ...; and (b) to the microchip database
-- company for that cat, if there is a change to any of the information prescribed under section 15 ..., within 7 days
-- after the change to the information. Penalty: a fine of $5 000." The prescribed information (regs 16, 17) includes my
-- name, addresses, telephone numbers and email, where the cat is kept, and its sterilisation status.
-- "within 7 days after" is reckoned with the day of the change not counted (the Interpretation Act 1984 s 61 is not
-- in the deposit; this is the encoder's reading). The Interpretation Act's rule moving a last day that falls on a
-- weekend or holiday is NOT applied.
@export By what day must I tell the local government and the microchip database of a change to my details (Cat Act 2011 (WA) s 25)?
GIVEN `the day of the change` IS A DATE @desc The day your details (for example your address) changed, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I give notice of the change` IS `the day of the change` PLUS 7

§§ `s 79(3)(h) and the Cat (Uniform Local Provisions) Regulations 2013 -- how many cats`

-- The Act itself sets no number. s 79(3)(h): a local law may be made "limiting the number of cats that may be kept at
-- premises, or premises of a particular type". The Uniform Local Provisions Regulations operate as local laws of every
-- local government (s 77; ULP reg 3):
-- reg 5: "a cat that is under 6 months of age is not to be included when calculating the number of cats ordinarily
-- kept at prescribed premises";
-- reg 4, 7: the "standard number of cats" is the local law's number, or, "If a member of a cat organisation is
-- ordinarily resident at prescribed premises, ... 3 times the number of cats that could be kept at the premises under
-- the local law";
-- reg 6(1): a resident "must ensure that the number of cats ordinarily kept at the premises is not more than the
-- standard number of cats for the premises. Penalty: a fine of $5 000."; (2) a defence where an approval for an
-- additional number is in effect and the total is within the standard number plus that additional number.
-- A "member of a cat organisation" is a current member of one of the four bodies in Cat Regulations 2012 reg 23(c).
-- Not encoded: reg 6(3) (premises operated by a reg 9 organisation) and reg 12 (the transitional defence).
DECLARE `How many cats` IS ONE OF
    `no number is set by the Act or the uniform regulations; a local law may set one (s 79(3)(h))`
    `at most this many cats aged 6 months or more`
        HAS `the number` IS A NUMBER

@export How many cats may I keep at my home (Cat Act 2011 (WA) s 79(3)(h); Cat (Uniform Local Provisions) Regulations 2013)?
GIVEN `a local law limits cats at my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a local law of your local government limits the number of cats that may be kept at premises like yours
      `the local law's number` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of cats the local law allows at your premises
      `a cat organisation member lives here` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a current member of one of the cat organisations in Cat Regulations 2012 reg 23(c) is ordinarily resident at the premises
      `additional cats approved` IS A NUMBER @desc The additional number of cats your local government has approved for the premises, 0 if none
GIVETH A `How many cats`
DECIDE `How many cats may I keep here` IS
    IF NOT `a local law limits cats at my home`
        THEN `no number is set by the Act or the uniform regulations; a local law may set one (s 79(3)(h))`
        ELSE `at most this many cats aged 6 months or more` (`the standard number` PLUS `additional cats approved`)
    WHERE
        `the standard number` MEANS
            IF `a cat organisation member lives here`
                THEN `the local law's number` TIMES 3
                ELSE `the local law's number`

§§ `Penalty lines, Sch 2 and ULP reg 13 -- what I can be fined`

-- Each duty above carries "Penalty: a fine of $5 000." Cat Regulations 2012 reg 30 and Sch 2 set a modified penalty
-- (the infringement notice amount) of $200 for items 1 (s 5(1)), 2 (s 6(1)), 4 (s 14(1)), 6 (s 18(1)), 8 (s 23(1)),
-- 9 (s 23(2)) and 11 (s 25); ULP reg 13(1) sets $200 for reg 6(1).
DECLARE `Offence` IS ONE OF
    `cat not registered (s 5(1))`
    `cat not wearing its tag in a public place (s 6(1))`
    `cat not microchipped (s 14(1))`
    `cat not sterilised (s 18(1))`
    `transferring a cat that is not microchipped (s 23(1))`
    `transferring a cat that is not sterilised (s 23(2))`
    `not giving notice of a change (s 25)`
    `keeping more than the standard number of cats (ULP reg 6(1))`

@export What is the most a court can fine me for this cat offence, in dollars?
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence` @desc The offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `keeping more than the standard number of cats (ULP reg 6(1))` THEN 5000
    OTHERWISE 5000

@export If I am given an infringement notice for this cat offence, how much is it, in dollars?
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence` @desc The offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is the infringement notice` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `keeping more than the standard number of cats (ULP reg 6(1))` THEN 200
    OTHERWISE 200
